common: give the memory-fit pass a ctx_other for MTP/draft heads

Problem
-------
Starting llama-server with an MTP draft head, e.g.

    llama-server --model Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Q8_0-00001-of-00006.gguf \
                 --model-draft mtp-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-shared-Q8_0.gguf \
                 --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 3 \
                 -ngl 99 -ncmoe 48 -c 155000 -b 2048 -ub 512 --flash-attn on

prints during startup:

    E llama_init_from_model: failed to initialize the context: qwen4exp requires ctx_other
      to be set (this warning is normal during memory fitting)
    W operator(): failed to measure the memory of the extra model, fitting without it:
      failed to create llama_context from model

Root cause
----------
common_init_result() (common/common.cpp:1304-1326) runs the automatic memory fit *before* the
target model is loaded, and describes the draft/MTP model to it as a common_fit_extra_model.
common_params_fit_impl()'s add_extra_memory() lambda (common/fit.cpp:204-257) measures that extra
model by loading it with no_alloc and building a throwaway llama_context for it
(common_get_device_memory_data_impl(), common/fit.cpp:64-70).

Draft heads whose GGUF has no token_embd/output of its own read those tensors from the target
model through llama_context_params::ctx_other (src/models/qwen4exp.cpp:26-35, and likewise
eagle3.cpp / dflash.cpp / gemma4-assistant.cpp).  llama_context::llama_context() rejects such a
model when ctx_other == nullptr (src/llama-context.cpp:155-162), llama_init_from_model() returns
nullptr, and common_get_device_memory_data_impl() throws.

The throw is caught in add_extra_memory() and the extra model is then accounted for with an
all-zero llama_device_memory_data (common/fit.cpp:225-231), i.e. the fit proceeds as if the draft
model needed no device memory at all.  Consequences:

  * when the fit is free to choose (-c / -ngl unset) it oversizes the KV cache / offloads too
    many layers, and the process OOMs later at runtime (typically in
    ggml_cuda_graph_evaluate_and_capture on the second request, once the CUDA graph is captured);
  * when -c / -ngl are pinned by the user, the deficit is invisible: the fit concludes
    "no changes needed" (common/fit.cpp:351-355) and never warns that the configuration cannot fit.

The whole failure is reported at W/E level but is worded as if it were benign, so it is easy to
miss.

Fix
---
Wire the target model's measurement context through to the extra model's measurement, so the
draft context can actually be built and measured:

  * common_get_device_memory_data_impl() gains an optional `common_fit_scratch_ctx * keep`
    out-parameter.  When given, the no_alloc model + context created for the measurement are
    handed to the caller instead of being freed immediately (and a previously kept pair is
    released first).  Default nullptr keeps every other caller unchanged.
  * common_params_fit_impl() keeps the scratch context of the most recent main-model measurement
    and add_extra_memory() passes it as extra->cparams->ctx_other.  All five main-model
    measurements that are followed by an add_extra_memory() now request it.  The pointer is
    cleared again right after the measurement so it can never dangle.
  * as a safety net, if the extra model still cannot be measured the fallback is now logged at
    ERROR level and states explicitly that device memory use is underestimated, with the flags
    to work around it.

This costs no extra model loads: the context that is kept alive is the one that was created for
the main model's measurement anyway.  Both models are loaded with no_alloc = true /
LLAMA_LOAD_MODE_NONE, so nothing is actually allocated on the device while both are alive.

Only common/fit.cpp is touched; no MTP-specific or public API code changes.

Apply with:  git apply patches/mtp-fit-ctx-other.patch   (from the repository root)

--- a/common/fit.cpp
+++ b/common/fit.cpp
@@ -26,6 +26,38 @@
     using std::runtime_error::runtime_error;
 };
 
+// [TAG_FIT_CTX_OTHER]
+// Some draft heads (MTP/NextN, EAGLE3, DFlash, Gemma4-Assistant) do not ship a token embedding and/or an
+// output tensor of their own - they read those from the target model through llama_context_params::ctx_other.
+// llama_init_from_model() refuses to build such a context when ctx_other == nullptr, so the memory fit has to
+// keep the measurement context of the main model alive and hand it to the measurement of the extra model.
+// Without it the extra model cannot be measured at all and would be silently assumed to need no memory.
+struct common_fit_scratch_ctx {
+    llama_model   * model = nullptr;
+    llama_context * ctx   = nullptr;
+
+    common_fit_scratch_ctx() = default;
+    common_fit_scratch_ctx(const common_fit_scratch_ctx &)             = delete;
+    common_fit_scratch_ctx & operator=(const common_fit_scratch_ctx &) = delete;
+
+    void reset() {
+        if (ctx) {
+            llama_free(ctx);
+            ctx = nullptr;
+        }
+        if (model) {
+            llama_model_free(model);
+            model = nullptr;
+        }
+    }
+
+    ~common_fit_scratch_ctx() {
+        reset();
+    }
+};
+
